uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:32:53-07:00","id":964926,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would suggest a fusion of Ascension's Right Hand, Demon Hunter X, Sorcerer, and Sorcerer (Revised) for a mortal campaign. There are a lot of advantages in ARH that can be used for superior human characters that I have allowed mortals to take (superior attributes and extra speed primarily, as almost everything else is blatantly inhuman). I would suggest the build rules from Sorcerer and, if you want to allow characters to be mundanes, convert the Path dots and Ritual dots to freebie points (which ends up being 44 extra freebie points). That way, you can have people make action heroes if they do not want to make psychics or sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:25:17-07:00","id":965228,"title":"","content":"dont forget Kinfolk unsung heroes had 3 Unique Numina, Hopefully spirit chasing is thoroughly fixed in the upcoming kinfolk book, as the idea has potential, but is too ill defined...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:36:43-07:00","id":966465,"title":"","content":"oh another related Question, how valuable or protected will someone with Numina usualy be.<br /> <br /> How badly will it hurt the Arcanum, Project Twilight,Pentex or the Mafia, to put a psychic or hedge magician their counting on out of commision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:11:39-07:00","id":966509,"title":"","content":"Revised is a pretty good source for your Psychic needs! I essentially use it as my go to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:14:59-07:00","id":966511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=966465#post966465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh another related Question, how valuable or protected will someone with Numina usualy be.<br /> <br /> How badly will it hurt the Arcanum, Project Twilight,Pentex or the Mafia, to put a psychic or hedge magician their counting on out of commision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcanum is filled with Sorcerers, so Psychics would be rarer and probably more missed. Project Twilight has government resources to find Psychics but they have a very limited supply. Mafia... just legends and family members that may know some tricks, or be connected to Glass Walkers or Giovanni. Pentex creates Psychics and boosts them with special Project Division. They also recruit and train Sorcerers. They can afford to send them to their dooms, but they are rarer then just normal Fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:53:55-07:00","id":966525,"title":"","content":"hmmmn thinking of a mission in a WTA game to take out a Project twilight Psychic, any ideas on a good Numina for her to know? Astral projection is the most obvious for being good at Recon, another is psychometry.<br /> <br /> any other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:14:03-07:00","id":966589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=966465#post966465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh another related Question, how valuable or protected will someone with Numina usualy be.<br /> <br /> How badly will it hurt the Arcanum, Project Twilight,Pentex or the Mafia, to put a psychic or hedge magician their counting on out of commision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on which numina and how powerful, it may hurt very baddly if one went out of commission. Especially if it was say their only one who could do XYZ..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=966525#post966525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn thinking of a mission in a WTA game to take out a Project twilight Psychic, any ideas on a good Numina for her to know? Astral projection is the most obvious for being good at Recon, another is psychometry.<br /> <br /> any other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Telepathy for knowing what someone's thinking or going to do.<br /> Precognition for knowing what they will be doing later, and where<br /> TK/PK for dealing damage..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:53:19-07:00","id":966641,"title":"","content":"Clairvoyance from Sorcerer (Revised) is one of the best Psychic Numina is the game, closely followed by Psychic Vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:16:06-07:00","id":966742,"title":"","content":"Telepathy, I'd like to see an approved version of it for X20, any ideas why they didnt give us one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:30:27-07:00","id":966921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=966641#post966641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clairvoyance from Sorcerer (Revised) is one of the best Psychic Numina is the game, closely followed by Psychic Vampirism.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the irks i have always had is how some game systems seem to mix up what clairvoyance IS.. Some think a clairvoyant is a precog, when it is far seeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:08:39-07:00","id":966943,"title":"","content":"Well, it is actually far sensing in Sorcerer (Revised). Precognition is its own power. The advantage of Clairvoyance over Astral Projection is that your consciousness stays in place, limiting your vulnerability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:16:42-07:00","id":967322,"title":"","content":"hmmmn another question in hunterts Hunted II it says with ST permission you may take Healing as a Psychic rather then hedge magic numina<br /> <br /> any reason someone would CHOOSE to have it as hedge magic, if psychic is a possiblety.<br /> <br /> As psychichs dont need herbs dolls etc.<br /> <br /> (As for magic in real life I got my mom a donald trump voodo doll and have a Maneki Neko and Dream catcher both in my apartment.<br /> <br /> All that stuff costs money I should know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:48:08-07:00","id":967954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=967322#post967322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn another question in hunterts Hunted II it says with ST permission you may take Healing as a Psychic rather then hedge magic numina<br /> <br /> any reason someone would CHOOSE to have it as hedge magic, if psychic is a possiblety.<br /> <br /> As psychichs dont need herbs dolls etc.<br /> <br /> (As for magic in real life I got my mom a donald trump voodo doll and have a Maneki Neko and Dream catcher both in my apartment.<br /> <br /> All that stuff costs money I should know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on your ST, characters can only be a hedge mage OR a psychic, rather than both. The alternative is that paths from your secondary set (e.g., psychic phenomena if you're a hedge mage) cost twice as much. Either way, if you take Healing as a psychic, you're either ruling out hedge magic paths altogether or accepting that you'll pay twice as much for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:48:57-07:00","id":971579,"title":"","content":"oh another Curiousity? <br /> <br /> how much BS do you think is Gospel in World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> Psychic hotlines, Chineese fortune cookies or CD's that will &quot;awaken your latent inner Power&quot; <br /> <br /> How much of that do you think is gospel? <br /> <br /> Note the last would be an EXCELLENT way in a Hunters Hunted Chronicle of allowing PC's to develop Psychic abilitys in spite of not previously having them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:02:56-07:00","id":971664,"title":"","content":"I think that much of it is BS. It is much easier to learn how to con people (or yourself) than it is to learn how to effectively use Numina. In real life, that was always one of the tragedies of dealing with the pagan community that I found, that many of them started to believe in their own magical powers so much that they ignored any evidence of their ineffectiveness, and would blame the failure of their magic to change the world on external factors (and this is coming from someone who is willing to believe that you have magic or psychic powers if you can show me something that is more than sheer coincidence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:24:27-07:00","id":971967,"title":"","content":"I know its BS in real life.<br /> <br /> I have a Maneki Neko, (A Jappanese cat Statue thats supposed to tell money &quot;Make yourself at home , you like it here, this is your home now.,) but money doesnt seem to listen to it<br /> <br /> I have a dream catcher , which is supposed to capture nightmares.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wasnt having many dreams to speak of to start with but the wolf on it is pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:42:52-07:00","id":972040,"title":"","content":"In my mind, anyone with Numina would likely fall in one of two categories. The first, and most common, category are casual practitioners who use their Numina to smooth out the edges of their life. The second, and rarer, category of dedicated practitioners who use their Numina to change the world for their own benefits or according to their own beliefs. In either case, they would have no interest in sharing their power with an unsympathetic world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T23:08:12-07:00","id":972362,"title":"","content":"Another thought.. With the prevalence in shows, films, novels etc of those with mind powers being hunted to either be forced to work FOR the government, or be killed so they can't be used against the government, how would the world at large handle people with actual psychic powers in a WOD setting..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:08:23-07:00","id":972529,"title":"","content":"Oh, I imagine that there would be a Special Projects Division (SPD) within the US government that registers and monitors people with Numina (Psychics and Sorcerers). They keep track of the low level talents and hire the high level talents for government work. If a high level talent does not want to work for the government, the government monitors them until they do something that allows them to be arrested, when they are sent to special federal prisons designed for people with unusual abilities. <br /> <br /> In my games, the SPD was formed in response to the Oklahoma City bombing and, by 2001, they were good enough to prevent 9/11 by having four SPD agents on each of the four flights. The ripple effects of that meant that a) the Bush Administration lacked a justification for war in Afghanistan and Iraq (leading to his defeat in 2004), b) President Kerry invaded North Korea after the first North Korean nuclear test in 2006, c) the East China Sea Incident (which resulted when the Chinese attempted to stop the US invasion of North Korea) in 2006 (resulting in the destruction of the Chinese Navy and Airforce), and d) the US spending the ten years rebuilding North Korea because no one else wants to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 09-19-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:28:46-07:00","id":972606,"title":"","content":"I'd go with SAD doing aggressive recruiting.<br /> <br /> but got into an argument with an idiot who wanted to heavily rewrite the setting once<br /> <br /> they argued that the settings deliberately contrived so the world cant &quot;adapt to whats in it&quot;<br /> <br /> Saying that Satelites should have rent the Garous veil asunder long ago.<br /> <br /> but back on psychics, Think we need precognition or Telepathy back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-19-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:48:51-07:00","id":972613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=972529#post972529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> d) the US spending the ten years rebuilding North Korea because no one else wants to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to remember where i read it, but i did see a novel based somewhat on that thought line.. 9/11 didn't happen, but we invaded NK instead, but i don't remember anything about rebuilding them afterwards..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:36:00-07:00","id":972728,"title":"","content":"I think that, if it had happened, rebuilding North Korea would have been required to prevent regional destabilization. Of course, that would have probably have costed hundreds of billions of dollars per year (in direct and indirect costs), so it would have occupied the attention of the USA for a while. Of course, there is a question of what the Chinese would have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T21:49:59-07:00","id":972941,"title":"","content":"Hence why iirc that novel went into we didn't do the nation rebuilding afterwards..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:46:10-07:00","id":974781,"title":"","content":"oh curious, how good is Pyrokenisis for Arsonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T21:17:14-07:00","id":974869,"title":"","content":"Very good. If used properly there SHOULDN'T be any evidence left over to use to profile the arsonist, such as &quot;favored drop spot, tools, accelerants&quot; and so on..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T21:41:25-07:00","id":974878,"title":"","content":"Especially since it does not cost anything to use, though I would make the argument that an Pyromaniac with Pyrokinesis would be caught really quickly by people uninterested by civil rights. A Pyrokinetic assassin or saboteur would, however, be probably be quite safe, as long as they made sure to focus their efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:50:58-07:00","id":975218,"title":"","content":"How so?? Are there any devices in common use strewn around to detect someone popping off a psychic power? If not, then how would they track him down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:14:26-07:00","id":975227,"title":"","content":"Pyromaniacs tend to return to the scene of the crime. They often have a compulsion to see their fire at work, meaning that they will likely be recognized after a few incidents (at least by anyone examining videos or pictures associated with the fire). Assassins and saboteurs rarely return to the scene of the crime, so they would be highly unlikely to be caught in a similar fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T18:44:42-07:00","id":975324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=967954#post967954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on your ST, characters can only be a hedge mage OR a psychic, rather than both. The alternative is that paths from your secondary set (e.g., psychic phenomena if you're a hedge mage) cost twice as much. Either way, if you take Healing as a psychic, you're either ruling out hedge magic paths altogether or accepting that you'll pay twice as much for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never understood excluding one or the other. They work fundamentally differently. Psychics use their will to to force things to do what they want(like lifting an object with their mind with telekinesis), while hedge mages use properties already inherit in the world(like brewing a potion from the magical properties of plants or using ritual items to move mana). I don't see how they'd be exclusive(unless psychic powers are run as a &quot;Genetic&quot; thing rather than something unlocked with high willpower and training. Then the psychic would be objectively better as there's nothing really stopping him from reciting the names of spirits over a magic circle to summon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T20:42:12-07:00","id":975357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975324#post975324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never understood excluding one or the other. They work fundamentally differently. Psychics use their will to to force things to do what they want(like lifting an object with their mind with telekinesis), while hedge mages use properties already inherit in the world(like brewing a potion from the magical properties of plants or using ritual items to move mana). I don't see how they'd be exclusive(unless psychic powers are run as a &quot;Genetic&quot; thing rather than something unlocked with high willpower and training. Then the psychic would be objectively better as there's nothing really stopping him from reciting the names of spirits over a magic circle to summon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know in some game systems, people with magical powers (hedge mages), often have a harder time developing or using psychics (mental).. So maybe the ST system took that to heart. Its either psychic numina, OR hedge magic, not both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:54:09-07:00","id":975447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975357#post975357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know in some game systems, people with magical powers (hedge mages), often have a harder time developing or using psychics (mental).. So maybe the ST system took that to heart. Its either psychic numina, OR hedge magic, not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably to stop people being OP. But it was Revised era, so that's pretty standard for that period. But it could also be a Paradigm thing: if you believe in hedge magic, you think that's how the supernatural works; and vice versa. It's an internal restriction you unconsciously place upon yourself. But, realistically, the Revised-era nerfing is probably more accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:48:21-07:00","id":975514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975324#post975324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never understood excluding one or the other. They work fundamentally differently. Psychics use their will to to force things to do what they want(like lifting an object with their mind with telekinesis), while hedge mages use properties already inherit in the world(like brewing a potion from the magical properties of plants or using ritual items to move mana). I don't see how they'd be exclusive(unless psychic powers are run as a &quot;Genetic&quot; thing rather than something unlocked with high willpower and training. Then the psychic would be objectively better as there's nothing really stopping him from reciting the names of spirits over a magic circle to summon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The double cost started out as a play balance thing for campaigns oriented around 'mortal' characters, and somewhat got 'stuck'.<br /> <br /> Weird thing is, WW in a couple of spots broke that rule themselves. (Via Ignis in Inquisition, and some of the suggested powers for organizations in Sorcerer Revised.)<br /> <br /> A lot of the STs I've played with ignore the double cost rule in mixed games, as long as the powers made sense for the character. (Astral Projection &amp; Emphamera would probably be OK, Hellfire and EctoSnot, not so much.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:18:02-07:00","id":975522,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that they were trying to group Numina into five categories: Chi (from Demon Hunter X), Faith (True Faith and the Paths from Inquisition), Mythic, Psychic, and Scientific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:46:29-07:00","id":975537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975522#post975522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that they were trying to group Numina into five categories: Chi (from Demon Hunter X), Faith (True Faith and the Paths from Inquisition), Mythic, Psychic, and Scientific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but doing so doesn't make sense if you also consider tremere thaum(which was developed from sorcery paths). Several of there thaum paths replicate psychic powers(like movement of the mind/telekinesis, lure of flames/pyrokinesis, etc.) and that seems to suggest that at one point, &quot;Psychic powers&quot; were just seen as another path of sorcery like healing or weather control.<br /> <br /> Besides, numina in general tend to be weaker than other supernatural's magic and a vampire can have the powers the different &quot;Classes&quot; of numina with their disciplines alone. Numina aren't &quot;power gamey&quot; the way that playing an abomination or having temporis is and making things exclusive puts mortals at such a severe disadvantage that it becomes frustrating to play in a mixed game. I ignore the &quot;Category&quot; thing in favor of having them be a step weaker than most creatures, but more diverse(like mage, only crossover friendly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:01:30-07:00","id":975662,"title":"","content":"Well, some Numina are really powerful (like True Faith), but they are (on average) weaker than the capabilities of major supernatural powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:08:04-07:00","id":975669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975447#post975447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably to stop people being OP. But it was Revised era, so that's pretty standard for that period. But it could also be a Paradigm thing: if you believe in hedge magic, you think that's how the supernatural works; and vice versa. It's an internal restriction you unconsciously place upon yourself. But, realistically, the Revised-era nerfing is probably more accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I lean to the 'internal paradigm thing..'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:03:40-07:00","id":975704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975669#post975669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lean to the 'internal paradigm thing..'</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very mage way of going about it. I do believe that restricts sorcerers to being nothing more than &quot;Lesser mages&quot; akin to ghouls, kinians, or kinfolk. A narrative loss if you think about it, sorcerers are ironically the best equipped being to deal with mages with their ridiculous amounts of counter magic. It would be nice to have something both equal and different from mages to kick them off their pedestal and show them that, no, they aren't special and the world does not revolve around them or their &quot;Consensus&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though that may be my own bias, I love the explorative and transhumanistic themes in mage, but absolutely hate how it loves to go the &quot;the universe revolves around humanity and everything else is crap cause we're so awesome&quot; route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:08:22-07:00","id":975707,"title":"","content":"Well, that is kind of why I allow every supernatural entity to develop Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:19:58-07:00","id":977109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/964485-psychic-numina?p=975522#post975522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that they were trying to group Numina into five categories: Chi (from Demon Hunter X), Faith (True Faith and the Paths from Inquisition), Mythic, Psychic, and Scientific.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish they had actually done this, codified it, and collected everything together in one book. That would make sense. I wouldn't charge double costs for additional categories, but I would rule that one is your primary category and thus the one the others can't exceed. Chi and Psychic powers would go well together, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:20:44-07:00","id":977110,"title":"","content":"Also, World of Darkness: Cyborg would be amazing... (without the need to buy multiple Mage supplements).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T07:28:53-07:00","id":977169,"title":"","content":"I think that the Augmented could be developed in any number of ways, from Golems created through Faith Numina to Cyborgs creates by Scientific Numina. I would actually create them using a modified Autonomy system, where their Willpower is slowly replaced by the Willpower of the 'Other' as they gain more and more power. Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}